    "reading": {
        "body": "AI companies are actively hiring for privacy and regulation roles, with six open positions across Cohere, Harvey, OpenAI, and Figure as of September 2026.\n\nThese roles cluster in two distinct areas. Four positions target regulatory and legal compliance, hired by generalist AI firms building systems that touch European markets. Two positions target technical privacy implementation, hired by OpenAI and Figure for internal engineering. The geographic split reflects this split: the legal roles cluster in Europe and London, while technical roles anchor to San Francisco and San Jose.\n\nThe hiring pattern suggests privacy has become an operational function rather than a legal afterthought. Companies are pairing counsel roles with engineering roles, which indicates privacy is now embedded in how systems are built, not applied after. The European concentration of counsel positions reflects the regulatory landscape there, not a uniform global hiring pattern.\n\nThis data captures only posted openings at major firms and does not measure total privacy hiring across the AI industry, smaller companies, or roles titled differently. It does not show whether these positions remained open, were filled, or represent growth versus replacement hiring.",
